  "summary": "Name the parts of the body and say what hurts with يُؤْلِمُنِي and تُؤْلِمُنِي.",
  "intro": "After the weekend in Alexandria, Daniel is back in class, but he does not feel well. Today you learn the main parts of the body. Several of them are feminine even without ة: يَد (hand), رِجْل (leg, foot), عَيْن (eye) and أُذُن (ear). To say what hurts, Arabic says 'it hurts me': يُؤْلِمُنِي رَأْسِي (my head hurts) for a masculine part, and تُؤْلِمُنِي يَدِي (my hand hurts) for a feminine one.",
